From 36c13e3c5948ecc03343dd73182b20db980a4b3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:13:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Emit float != as the unordered fcmp une (nuc-iron-doom
 ISSUE-013)

C, Rust and IEEE 754 all make != true when either operand is NaN; the
ordered fcmp one made (!= x x) false for NaN. The compiler's own source
has a float !=, so this moves the bootstrap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8hzrZakM3KWb32SpqKh
---
 docs/types.md        |  2 +-
 src/nucleusc.nuc     |  2 +-
 tests/suite-doom.nuc | 12 ++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/types.md b/docs/types.md
index 66eb768..69efed0 100644
